# class: clearances
# origin: audits/2026-10-18-first-contact.md T2 (first-contact-plans/5-townhouse.arch L0: the sofa 250 mm in front of
#   g_o_hl; living and kitchen measured from g_patio); README PS0.10
# expect: W_PATH_TOO_NARROW
# status: done
# fact: the sofa (x 2400-3300, y 5000-7000) stands 250 mm in front of o_hl (w_v face x 2150, y 5500-6500) over its
#   full width; describe measures Living and Dining from d_patio (1540 mm), so lint is silent; with d_patio made a
#   window, lint gives W_PATH_TOO_NARROW 200 mm for "Living" and "Dining". Since PS0.10 the walk is judged from the
#   main entrance (d_front, the door into the hall), so lint reports "Living" 200 mm as it stands, with no site;
#   "Dining" opens onto the garden through d_patio itself, which is a way into it, so it is not reported
plan "Sofa across the hall opening, masked by the patio door" {
  units mm
  grid 50
  wall id=shell exterior thickness 250 { (0,0) (5500,0) (5500,8000) (0,8000) close }
  wall id=w_h partition thickness 100 { (0,4000) (5500,4000) }
  wall id=w_v partition thickness 100 { (2100,4000) (2100,8000) }
  room id=r_din at (0,0) size 5500x4000 label "Dining" uses dining
  room id=r_hall at (0,4000) size 2100x4000 label "Hall" uses hall
  room id=r_liv at (2100,4000) size 3400x4000 label "Living" uses living
  door id=d_front at (1000,8000) width 900 wall shell swing into r_hall
  opening id=o_hl at (2100,6000) width 1000 wall w_v
  opening id=o_ld at (3800,4000) width 1800 wall w_h
  door id=d_patio sliding at (4400,0) width 1600 wall shell
  window at (1200,0) width 1200 wall shell
  window at (3800,8000) width 2000 wall shell
  furniture sofa at (2400,5000) size 900x2000 label "Sofa" rotate 270
}
